{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/266088-you-re-suddenly-rich","id":266088,"title":"You're suddenly rich!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-26T05:04:25-07:00","id":266088,"title":"You're suddenly rich!","content":"So you win the two hundred million dollar lottery. Good for you. It's more money than you know what to do with, though, and keeping it all seems kind of obscene when there are so many people in the world who need help, so, civic-minded soul that you are, you decide to donate some fraction of your money to charity. What cause do you pick?<br /> <br /> My first inclination is education. I don't know a specific charity, but kids need better books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T05:23:39-07:00","id":266097,"title":"","content":"I think it might be wise to check out any charity before giving anything to it. A starting point might be here; <a href=\"http://www.charitynavigator.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Charity Navigator</a>. Another; <a href=\"http://www.charitywatch.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Charity Watch</a>, and others as well; <a href=\"http://www.bbb.org/charity-reviews/national/\" target=\"_blank\">Better Business Bureau</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.guidestar.org/organizations/13-4148824/charity-navigator.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">Guidestar</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T05:56:52-07:00","id":266109,"title":"","content":"Divide it in half.<br /> <br /> One half shall be connected to some financial advisors who will be given a lot of latitude to invest and manage it, preferably towards things that will promote economic stimulation and charitable causes.<br /> <br /> Of the other half, I shall reserve fifty grand for my personal uses, whatever else is needed to allow my parents (and maybe a few other relatives) to pay off their debts, and the remainder shall be preserved against the future such that I can contribute to my own research funding.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I did not read past the first half of the first line of the first post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T06:19:25-07:00","id":266116,"title":"","content":"Well, I probably wouldn't be very charitable myself. Not that I would have an extravagant life either. I've always been somewhat poor, and even when I was making decent wages I was always very aware that it could all go away pretty quick. (and it kinda did)<br /> To be able to give to charity I would have to be at first comfortable with what I have and the ongoing income.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T06:28:50-07:00","id":266119,"title":"","content":"If my first concern was to get rid of the money as fast as possible, I'd probably give most of it to the Catholic Church, and put the rest towards medical research and green energy projects.<br /> <br /> If my concern was to use the money as effectively as possible, I'd use it to start a Foundation of some kind, with the goal of supporting long-term, wide-scale social improvement projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T07:16:40-07:00","id":266135,"title":"","content":"I am partial to the support of education, and helping the homeless, so I'd use the money to pay some tuition and buy some people a house (and I'll be honest, all the people I have in mind are people I know personally... I'm not a person that trusts &quot;charitable organizations&quot; because they appear to be incredibly inefficient with the funds donated to them, at best).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T10:14:29-07:00","id":266274,"title":"","content":"The problem I'm having is that there are SO MANY causes which I think need more funding. Some of the ones I've thought of: suicide prevention for LGBT teens, the survivors of our raping and pillaging in the middle east, education, etc.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'd start a lobbying firm to try to get some laws changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T10:34:12-07:00","id":266283,"title":"","content":"Have you won a $200 million lottery and are trying to figure out what to do with your money, Jim?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T11:05:56-07:00","id":266310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/266088-you-re-suddenly-rich?p=266274#post266274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I'm having is that there are SO MANY causes which I think need more funding. Some of the ones I've thought of: suicide prevention for LGBT teens, the survivors of our raping and pillaging in the middle east, education, etc.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'd start a lobbying firm to try to get some laws changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if I seriously sat down and thought about all the organizations I think should be donated to, that entire two-hundred million would disappear pretty quick. That stands doubly true is I talked with you(or anyone else here) about it.<br /> <br /> Which isn't necessarily a lamentable thing, except I'm also a wee bit greedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T11:21:21-07:00","id":266313,"title":"","content":"I'd built an Off-the-Grid Victorian Mansion, pay off my debts, learn some things, travel, and supply libraries with banned books and homeless youth a place to sleep at night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T12:23:44-07:00","id":266366,"title":"","content":"First, I bank $20 million in a savings account. Even a low-interest account will yield about $100,000 a year in interest. Plenty for me to live on. I won the damn money, I'm not going back to my shit job so everybody ELSE can reap the rewards.<br /> <br /> Second, I create my OWN charitable foundation so <b>I </b>get to decide when, where, how much goes to what. Ultimately, what I would like to create is a think tank with some decent funding to keep their ideas from just going off into the ether and instead turning them into realities. Including creating some things that can be patented and sold so the well won't dry out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T14:15:11-07:00","id":266432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/266088-you-re-suddenly-rich#post266088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you win the two hundred million dollar lottery. Good for you. It's more money than you know what to do with, though, and keeping it all seems kind of obscene when there are so many people in the world who need help, so, civic-minded soul that you are, you decide to donate some fraction of your money to charity. What cause do you pick?<br /> <br /> My first inclination is education. I don't know a specific charity, but kids need better books.</div> </div> </div> </div>My objection is the claim that 200 million is more than I know what to do with.<br /> <br /> I invest it in a variety of stable secure growth pools, which should yield something in the 5-10 million/year pre-tax range. In a range of countries and industries for preference.<br /> <br /> From that base, I take enough to have a very comfortable standard of living as well as the durable requirements of life... Basically buy house that's about 2500 square feet, or finally build up my dream house outside the city a bit, get a new car every 3-5 years and take enough to have a very comfortable lifestyle... say 100,000 post tax every year. <br /> <br /> From there, I re-invest much of the money to offset inflation plus a percentage point or two (just in case there's an abnormal inflation spike).<br /> <br /> This is going to leave me with anywhere from 2-6 million range per year.<br /> <br /> <br /> With that I delve into putting my money into quietly helping out friends and family. Friend wants to open a comic and game shop, has a good idea but lacks capital? Bam, capital to start the shop. Kid has brains and can't swing the cost of college? Bam, costs covered or possibly just a sane terms loan.<br /> <br /> From there, I would start searching out reliable people willing to do a few specific charity projects. Specifically as an effort to offer the homeless the basic tools/needs to be able to recover in life, be it digital and physical mailing addresses, food, interview clothing, general progressive assistance.<br /> <br /> From that point I'd move on more to helping with cheap agriculture automation and possible see if I could help out with lowering the cost and increasing the functionality of prosthetic limbs and other functionality replacements... the current state of what is acceptable is abysmal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T15:16:21-07:00","id":266471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/266088-you-re-suddenly-rich?p=266283#post266283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you won a $200 million lottery and are trying to figure out what to do with your money, Jim?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I've decided I want to be independently wealthy, so I buy a ticket any time the jackpot gets that high.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/266088-you-re-suddenly-rich?p=266432#post266432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My objection is the claim that 200 million is more than I know what to do with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, just accept the premise of the hypothetical, ya stickler.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T15:22:45-07:00","id":266474,"title":"","content":"I collect every Warhammer Fantasy and 40K army. All of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T20:57:41-07:00","id":267953,"title":"","content":"I would give all of the money to Beyonce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:08:22-07:00","id":267958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/266088-you-re-suddenly-rich?p=267953#post267953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would give all of the money to Beyonce.</div> </div> </div> </div>...What? Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:14:59-07:00","id":267960,"title":"","content":"She's arguably the most important and hardest working woman of color in the entertainment industry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:23:28-07:00","id":267963,"title":"","content":"Thank you Kanye West.<br /> <br /> In other news, the rest of the human population has real problems, particularly the women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:32:09-07:00","id":267964,"title":"","content":"It's my belief that Beyonce would use that money to make music that inspires people to rise above their circumstances even more than it did previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T02:36:21-07:00","id":268116,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck\">Odd_Canuck</a> broke it down really well. I might do things a little differently here and there but if we talk about the core it is the same. One thing that's very important to me is privacy, I would take pains to ensure that my rise in wealth would look gradual and not spontaneous.<br /> <br /> Like it or not everyone will look at you differently, family and friends. If it is gradual you'll be able to retain a bit of your formal life, since with 200M no matter how hard you try, your life will NEVER be the same again.<br /> <br /> In my country, people who became millionaires through lottery, winning 15M or in some cases 50M \u20ac, had their lives ruined. By many different variables, but for me one of the worst was the harassment of people, strangers, friends, neighbours, etc. who for some stupid reason felt they were entitled to a share of the wealth and became violent when denied.<br /> <br /> I don't believe in charity organizations, but I like the way Odd_Canuck put it and there are some friends I would love to help, who are struggling and just need a break and at the moment I'm powerless to do anything.<br /> <br /> @Leaper: I just hope you are trolling because never before have I read such retard thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T06:06:07-07:00","id":268201,"title":"","content":"I recall reading a statistic that most of those that hit the lottery and win big, are broke in a couple of years. (So I'm taking notes here, because some day....just in case)<br /> <br /> Beyonc\u00e9 could always use another mansion...Although were I to look to a celebrity for inspiration, I'd look at Angelina Jolie and by extension Brad Pitt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T08:48:15-07:00","id":268282,"title":"","content":"I believe that to be true. There are stories on every country of EU of someone who won millions and end up broke and living on charity. It's good to be rich, but being middle class (or under) and win an obscene amount, like the 200M of this post for sake of argument, it's in most case worse than winning nothing at all. It's too much too sudden. You don't build up on it, you are hit by a freight train and overwhelmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T14:11:13-07:00","id":268525,"title":"","content":"Dementia research. Cancer has hit close to home in the past too, but Dementia is a hard thing to have going on with someone. And It seem so much more prevalent now days(whether that is because we are more aware or if it actually happens more is still being discussed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}